# The parse sidecar's worker (ADR 0097): its sandbox runs java @/app/parse.options once per connection, the connection as
# the worker's stdin and stdout, with an empty environment. These are attach/Parsers' WORKER_FLAGS, which its in-container
# child uses too (ParseOptionsTest compares them), then the classpath, the main class and --from-stream. So the
# sandbox's command line carries nothing from desk-agent, and these stay versioned with the code.
# - The default CDS archive only (-Xshare:auto), as the child: desk-agent.jsa is trained for desk-agent, not the worker.
# - The security manager is allowed so worker/Sandbox can install itself, a second layer while desk-agent is on JDK 21.
#   Without it the worker refuses to read.
# - The JVM's own output goes to stderr (discarded), so stdout is only the answer: HotSpot prints its out-of-memory exit
#   and unified logging's warnings on stdout otherwise, and desk-agent would read them as a first line that isn't one.
-Xmx72m
-Xms8m
-Xss512k
-XX:+UseSerialGC
-XX:TieredStopAtLevel=1
-XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=96m
-XX:+ExitOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:-HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:-CreateCoredumpOnCrash
-XX:ErrorFile=/dev/null
-XX:-UsePerfData
-XX:+DisableAttachMechanism
-XX:+DisplayVMOutputToStderr
-Xlog:disable
-Xlog:all=warning:stderr
-Xshare:auto
-Djava.awt.headless=true
-Djava.security.manager=allow
-Dma.attach.debug=false
-cp
/app/desk-agent.jar
com.minimalistalliance.desk.agent.attach.worker.ParseWorker
--from-stream
